Hi!&nbsp;<br />
<br />
Soon you will be receiving your tax bills for your Texas property/properties.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
Taxes in the state of Texas are considered LATE if not paid BEFORE January 31st of the following year. It is your responsibility to pay these taxes.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
Texas tax sites are only update once or twice a year with new owner information. So it is a real possibility that you will not receive a bill in the mail.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
All of us want to keep you informed as much as possible as to avoid any late penalties. The name on these sites could still be under the Memphis Invest GP name but if you own it - you are responsible for the taxes. You can pay this bill even if it&#39;s not under your name as yet. Eventually the state will update their records. I have been told it can take up to 6-12 months.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
If your property is owned by your IRA then you will need to contact and notify your IRA company that these taxes need to be paid.